# Infrastructure Layer

Persistence adapters, controllers (FastAPI routers), and DTOs — the "how".

Rules:
- Controllers (FastAPI routers) in `<context>_controller.py` — register
  endpoints, call use cases, return responses.
- `<context>_repository.py` implements the domain repository interface
  against a real database (SQLAlchemy, Tortoise, or in-memory).
- `<context>_schema.py` defines Pydantic request/response DTOs — keep them
  here, NOT in domain.
- Infrastructure may import from `domain/`, `application/`, `shared/`,
  and `config/`.

Files per bounded context:
- `<context>_controller.py` — FastAPI router (endpoints)
- `<context>_repository.py` — persistence adapter implementing the interface
- `<context>_schema.py` — Pydantic DTOs (optional, gated on `hasValidation`)
